01:00:14,334 --> 01:00:17,400
I GET SO SICK OF THIS
HOLLYWOOD CRAP.

1280
01:00:17,434 --> 01:00:18,400
THAT'S WHAT IT IS.

1281
01:00:18,434 --> 01:00:19,400
I LIKE REAL.

1282
01:00:19,434 --> 01:00:20,868
I AGREE.

1283
01:00:20,901 --> 01:00:22,934
I'M AN OLD FARM GIRL
AND I LIKE REAL.

1284
01:00:22,968 --> 01:00:26,367
SO THAT'S WHY I'M WEARING
ALL THESE WIGS!

1285
01:00:27,667 --> 01:00:30,334
♪ GLORIA, GLORIA ♪

1286
01:00:31,234 --> 01:00:33,834
♪ GLORIA, GLORIA ♪

1287
01:00:33,868 --> 01:00:35,501
Tammy: I WAS
A LITTLE DISCONCERTED.

1288
01:00:35,534 --> 01:00:37,467
THEY LOOK AT YOUR FACE
AND FIGURE OUT THAT

1289
01:00:37,501 --> 01:00:38,634
YOU'VE GOT TO COCK IT
THIS WAY TO LOOK GOOD.

1290
01:00:38,667 --> 01:00:39,634
THIS WAY?

1291
01:00:39,667 --> 01:00:42,801
Greg: YEAH.
THAT'S PERFECT.

1292
01:00:43,667 --> 01:00:45,467
I DID HAVE TO TAKE
A LOT OF THE MASCARA OFF,

1293
01:00:45,501 --> 01:00:49,534
WHICH WAS OK WITH ME
BECAUSE IT ENDED UP
BEING WHAT I THOUGHT

1294
01:00:49,567 --> 01:00:50,868
A VERY GOOD LOOK FOR ME.

1295
01:00:50,901 --> 01:00:51,968
♪ GLORIA ♪

1296
01:00:52,067 --> 01:00:53,801
[SINGING IN LATIN]

1297
01:00:53,834 --> 01:00:55,567
I WANTED TO LEAVE
THE PHOTO SESSION

1298
01:00:55,601 --> 01:00:57,567
AND GO DIRECTLY
TO THE PLASTIC SURGEON.

1299
01:00:57,601 --> 01:01:00,133
COULD I HAVE AFFORDED IT,
I WOULD HAVE,

1300
01:01:00,167 --> 01:01:01,534
BUT UNFORTUNATELY
I'M STILL HERE.

1301
01:01:01,567 --> 01:01:04,801
RuPaul: THE NEXT DAY
TAMMY WENT TO USA NETWORKS

1302
01:01:04,834 --> 01:01:06,434
TO PITCH HER IDEAS
FOR TV SHOWS

1303
01:01:06,467 --> 01:01:08,734
TO NETWORK EXECUTIVE
STEVEN CHOW,

1304
01:01:08,767 --> 01:01:11,133
CREATOR OF COPS AND STUDS.

1305
01:01:11,167 --> 01:01:12,133
HELLO.
WELL, HI, STEVEN!

1306
01:01:12,167 --> 01:01:14,100
HOW ARE YOU?
NICE TO MEET YOU.
I'M TAMMY.

1307
01:01:14,133 --> 01:01:15,834
NICE TO MEET YOU.
HI. HAVE A SEAT.

1308
01:01:15,868 --> 01:01:17,501
OK. THANK YOU.

1309
01:01:17,534 --> 01:01:18,501
SO YOU HERE
TO PITCH SOMETHING.

1310
01:01:18,534 --> 01:01:20,567
WELL, YOU'RE HERE TO PITCH,
SO START, RIGHT?

1311
01:01:20,601 --> 01:01:22,334
OK. WELL, NO, I--

1312
01:01:22,367 --> 01:01:23,467
I'VE GOT 3 IDEAS, STEVEN,

1313
01:01:23,501 --> 01:01:26,934
AND THEN I WOULD LIKE
TO KNOW WHAT YOU
SEE ME AS DOING.

1314
01:01:26,968 --> 01:01:29,167
BUT ONE OF MY IDEAS
IS A CHILDREN'S SHOW,

1315
01:01:29,200 --> 01:01:32,267
WHERE WE TALK TO PUPPETS
AND WE TALK TO THE KIDS,

1316
01:01:32,300 --> 01:01:34,701
AND THEN KIDS
TALKING TO PUPPETS
ABOUT THEIR PROBLEMS

1317
01:01:34,734 --> 01:01:37,047
AND THEIR CONCERNS
AND THINGS WHICH BOTHER THEM.

1318
01:01:37,067 --> 01:01:41,300
IT WOULD BE A FUN SHOW
WITH SOME SERIOUS PARTS
ONCE IN A WHILE, YOU KNOW.

1319
01:01:41,334 --> 01:01:43,234
IT'S A WAY TO GO.
I'M NOT SURE IT'S--

1320
01:01:43,267 --> 01:01:46,934
BUT WHAT ABOUT PUPPETS AND...
EVERYBODY LOVES PUPPETS.
EVEN ADULTS...

1321
01:01:46,968 --> 01:01:47,934
SURE.

1322
01:01:47,968 --> 01:01:49,367
LOVE PUPPETS.

1323
01:01:49,400 --> 01:01:51,067
UH-HUH.

1324
01:01:51,100 --> 01:01:52,133
I HAVE ANOTHER ONE.

1325
01:01:52,167 --> 01:01:53,834
TEENAGERS NEED SOMETHING
REALLY SPECIAL.

1326
01:01:53,868 --> 01:01:56,367
THEY NEED A FORMAT
FOR A LOT OF THINGS.

1327
01:01:56,400 --> 01:01:58,634
AND THEY HAVE NO WAY--
THE BIGGEST THING
THEY ALWAYS SAY,

1328
01:01:58,667 --> 01:02:01,767
"WELL, HOW DO WE GET
ANYONE TO LISTEN TO US?"

1329
01:02:01,801 --> 01:02:04,534
AND I WOULD JUST LOVE
TO GIVE THEM THAT CHANCE.

1330
01:02:04,567 --> 01:02:05,634
AND GO WHERE THEY GO.

1331
01:02:05,667 --> 01:02:08,400
I WOULD LIKE TO GO
TO THE PIERCING PARLORS
WITH THEM.

1332
01:02:08,434 --> 01:02:10,200
I'D LIKE TO GO TO
THE TATTOO PLACES WITH THEM.

1333
01:02:10,234 --> 01:02:12,100
JUST DO EVERYTHING
THAT TEENAGERS DO.

1334
01:02:12,133 --> 01:02:14,868
AND--AND YOU WOULD
CALL THIS SHOW WHAT?

1335
01:02:14,901 --> 01:02:16,801
TAMMY'S TERRIFIC TEENS

1336
01:02:16,834 --> 01:02:18,267
WOULD BE A FUN TITLE.

1337
01:02:18,300 --> 01:02:19,267
AND, UM...

1338
01:02:19,300 --> 01:02:20,501
ALL RIGHT.
NO, I'M JUST CURIOUS.

1339
01:02:20,534 --> 01:02:23,901
YEAH, YEAH, WE'D
PROBABLY HAVE TO COME UP
WITH SOMETHING FUN.

1340
01:02:23,934 --> 01:02:26,167
AND THEN I'VE GOT ONE MORE.
HA HA HA.

1341
01:02:26,200 --> 01:02:28,167
OK. NO, NO, NO. I MEAN,
WE'LL CIRCLE BACK.

1342
01:02:28,200 --> 01:02:29,834
OK. MEDICINE TODAY
WITH TAMMY FAYE.

1343
01:02:29,868 --> 01:02:34,133
PEOPLE NEED TO KNOW
WHAT IS AVAILABLE, YOU KNOW,

1344
01:02:34,167 --> 01:02:35,968
IN THE MARKET THAT'S
COMING UP NEW

1345
01:02:36,067 --> 01:02:39,047
AND WHAT IS AVAILABLE--
THE OLD THINGS THAT WORK
IN MEDICINE.

1346
01:02:39,067 --> 01:02:40,100
UM...

1347
01:02:40,133 --> 01:02:41,434
I MEAN, I'D LIKE TO GO
SIT WITH ALZHEIMER'S PATIENTS

1348
01:02:41,467 --> 01:02:43,100
AND EXPLAIN ALL--
HAVE THE DOCTORS
EXPLAIN ALZHEIMER'S.

1349
01:02:43,133 --> 01:02:44,868
AY YI YI.

1350
01:02:44,901 --> 01:02:46,868
I DON'T KNOW.
I'M JUST THROWING THESE OUT.

1351
01:02:46,901 --> 01:02:48,501
IT'S JUST IDEAS
THAT I'VE HAD FROM BEING ON--

1352
01:02:48,534 --> 01:02:51,200
YOU KNOW, JUST IDEAS THAT
HAVE BEEN SWIMMING AROUND
IN MY HEAD.

1353
01:02:51,234 --> 01:02:54,133
WHAT DO YOU SEE ME DOING,
STEVE?

1354
01:02:54,167 --> 01:02:55,133
YOU'RE THE--
I DON'T KNOW.

1355
01:02:55,167 --> 01:02:56,767
YOU'RE THE...
I MEAN, I DON'T...

1356
01:02:56,801 --> 01:02:59,400
EXPERT.
I MEAN, I THINK--
I SUSPECT, AND I'M

1357
01:02:59,434 --> 01:03:01,467
MAKING A STATEMENT
THAT MAY OR MAY NOT
BE TRUE,

1358
01:03:01,501 --> 01:03:05,701
BUT I THINK THAT
YOU WANT TO BE
ON THE AIR.

1359
01:03:05,734 --> 01:03:07,367
YOU REALLY LIKE BEING
IN FRONT OF THE CAMERA.

1360
01:03:07,400 --> 01:03:09,634
WELL, I LOVE THE CAM--
I DO LOVE THE CAMERA.

1361
01:03:09,667 --> 01:03:11,133
BECAUSE I THINK--
WHY?

1362
01:03:11,167 --> 01:03:12,133
BECAUSE IT'S A PERSON.

1363
01:03:12,167 --> 01:03:13,567
I'VE NEVER BEEN
IN FRONT OF THE CAMERA

1364
01:03:13,601 --> 01:03:15,501
SO I'M NOT SURE THAT
I UNDERSTAND THE APPEAL.

1365
01:03:15,534 --> 01:03:17,200
BECAUSE IT'S PEOPLE.
IT'S NOT A CAMERA.

1366
01:03:17,234 --> 01:03:19,267
IT'S PEOPLE.
IT'S SOMEONE TO TALK TO.

1367
01:03:19,300 --> 01:03:20,634
I--I DON'T KNOW,
YOU KNOW.

1368
01:03:20,667 --> 01:03:21,934
YOU'RE ON YOUR OWN.
I CAN'T HELP--

1369
01:03:21,968 --> 01:03:24,334
I CAN'T--I MEAN,
I HAVE NO PLACE
FOR A TALK SHOW.

1370
01:03:24,367 --> 01:03:25,334
I UNDERSTAND THAT, STEVEN.

1371
01:03:25,367 --> 01:03:26,934
I SHOULD WALK YOU
DOWNSTAIRS TO LIFETIME

1372
01:03:26,968 --> 01:03:29,133
WHICH ABOUT 15 FLOORS
BELOW US RIGHT NOW.

1373
01:03:29,167 --> 01:03:32,634
WELL, MAYBE YOU COULD
PUT MY NAME IN AT LIFETIME,

1374
01:03:32,667 --> 01:03:35,067
SEE MAYBE SOMEONE
WOULD BE INTERESTED THERE.

1375
01:03:35,100 --> 01:03:37,100
I WOULD REALLY
APPRECIATE THAT, STEVEN.

1376
01:03:37,133 --> 01:03:40,467
[TELEPHONE RINGING]

1377
01:03:41,868 --> 01:03:43,534
Woman: GOOD AFTERNOON,
LIFETIME.

1378
01:03:43,567 --> 01:03:45,634
IS DAWN THERE?
IT'S STEVEN CHOW.

1379
01:03:45,667 --> 01:03:46,767
RuPaul: THE CALL TO LIFETIME

1380
01:03:46,801 --> 01:03:49,734
WENT UNRETURNED, AND TAMMY
FOUND OTHER NETWORKS

1381
01:03:49,767 --> 01:03:53,667
UNWILLING TO MEET
AND DISCUSS HER
TELEVISION COMEBACK.

1382
01:03:53,701 --> 01:03:57,801
SO SHE RETURNED
TO THE DESERT...

1383
01:04:00,901 --> 01:04:03,334
Tammy: COME ON, MUFFIN.

1384
01:04:03,367 --> 01:04:05,300
[WHISTLING]

1385
01:04:05,334 --> 01:04:06,300
MUFFIN?

1386
01:04:06,334 --> 01:04:09,300
RuPaul: ALONE,
WITH HER DOLLS,

1387
01:04:09,334 --> 01:04:10,300
HER DOGS...

1388
01:04:10,334 --> 01:04:12,067
YOU STAY, RIGHT THERE.

1389
01:04:12,100 --> 01:04:14,100
AND HER FAITH.

1390
01:04:14,133 --> 01:04:17,567
♪ HALLELUJAH ♪

1391
01:04:17,601 --> 01:04:21,067
♪ HALLELUJAH ♪

1392
01:04:21,100 --> 01:04:23,667
♪ HALLELUJAH ♪

1393
01:04:23,701 --> 01:04:26,367
Man: MY WIFE AND I
RAN INTO TAMMY FAYE,

1394
01:04:26,400 --> 01:04:28,734
AND WE'D MET HER PRIOR
AND I SAID,

1395
01:04:28,767 --> 01:04:31,200
"WELL, TAMMY FAYE,
WHY DON'T YOU COME
TO CHURCH?"

1396
01:04:31,234 --> 01:04:33,734
AND SHE SAID,
"OH, I COULDN'T
COME TO CHURCH

1397
01:04:33,767 --> 01:04:35,200
BECAUSE I'VE BEEN
DIVORCED."

1398
01:04:35,234 --> 01:04:37,901
WHEN WE DO KIND
OF MISS THE MARK,

1399
01:04:37,934 --> 01:04:41,100
WHAT GOD HAS TO SAY IS
COME BACK.

1400
01:04:41,133 --> 01:04:44,534
Tammy: GOING BACK TO CHURCH
WAS VERY FRIGHTENING FOR ME.

1401
01:04:44,567 --> 01:04:46,167
BUT AS I WALKED
IN OUR CHURCH,

1402
01:04:46,200 --> 01:04:50,133
PASTOR JEFF CAME AND PUT THOSE
GREAT BIG OL' ARMS
AROUND ME,

1403
01:04:50,167 --> 01:04:53,968
AND HE SAID, "TAMMY FAYE,
WE WANT YOU HERE."

1404
01:04:54,067 --> 01:04:55,334
AND ALL OF A SUDDEN,

1405
01:04:55,367 --> 01:04:58,133
I BELONGED
AT PASTOR JEFF'S CHURCH.

1406
01:04:58,167 --> 01:05:01,834
RuPaul: TODAY TAMMY
LEADS THE CHOIR

1407
01:05:01,868 --> 01:05:04,067
AND PLAYS
FRANK SINATRA'S ORGAN,

1408
01:05:04,100 --> 01:05:05,501
A BEQUEST TO THE CHURCH.

1409
01:05:05,534 --> 01:05:09,801
Tammy: YOU CANNOT GO FORWARD
LOOKING IN THE REARVIEW
MIRROR OF YOUR LIFE.

1410
01:05:09,834 --> 01:05:12,100
JUST DROP IT ALL
AND MOVE ON

1411
01:05:12,133 --> 01:05:14,067
AND IT'S THE ONLY WAY IN LIFE

1412
01:05:14,100 --> 01:05:18,934
THAT YOU WILL EVER FIND
PEACE, JOY AND VICTORY.

1413
01:05:25,133 --> 01:05:27,801
[GRRR]

1414
01:05:27,834 --> 01:05:30,300
RuPaul: FINALLY TAMMY
HAD THE CONFIDENCE

1415
01:05:30,334 --> 01:05:31,534
TO SING AGAIN.

1416
01:05:31,567 --> 01:05:35,601
SHE ACCEPTED AN INVITATION
TO SING AT ORAL ROBERTS
UNIVERSITY

1417
01:05:35,634 --> 01:05:38,367
IN THE HEART
OF BIBLE COUNTRY.

1418
01:05:38,400 --> 01:05:40,167
Tammy: I DREADED GOING BACK

1419
01:05:40,200 --> 01:05:44,100
BECAUSE THE CHRISTIAN
COMMUNITY HAD BEEN
SO UNKIND TO US,

1420
01:05:44,133 --> 01:05:47,167
AND I FELT WE HAD
BEEN JUDGED SO UNFAIRLY

1421
01:05:47,200 --> 01:05:49,801
BY OUR BROTHERS AND SISTERS
IN THE LORD.

1422
01:05:49,834 --> 01:05:56,634
TO MAKE THE TRIP, TAMMY
ALSO HAD TO OVERCOME
HER FEAR OF FLYING.

1423
01:05:56,667 --> 01:05:59,767
I USED TO BE HORRIBLY
NERVOUS ON AIRPLANES.

1424
01:05:59,801 --> 01:06:03,434
I'M ONLY SLIGHTLY NERVOUS
ON AN AIRPLANE NOW,

1425
01:06:03,467 --> 01:06:05,133
AND IT'S GETTING BETTER
ALL THE TIME.

1426
01:06:05,167 --> 01:06:06,667
[THUNDER]

1427
01:06:06,701 --> 01:06:08,901
RuPaul: BAD WEATHER GROUNDED
THE PLANE IN DALLAS.

1428
01:06:08,934 --> 01:06:12,047
Man: LADIES AND GENTLEMEN,
THIS IS THE CAPTAIN SPEAKING.

1429
01:06:12,067 --> 01:06:13,133
THE GUST FRONT
HAS JUST HIT,

1430
01:06:13,167 --> 01:06:16,701
SO WE ARE GOING
TO BE SITTING HERE
FOR A LITTLE WHILE.

1431
01:06:16,734 --> 01:06:19,601
I DON'T LIKE THIS AT ALL.

1432
01:06:21,534 --> 01:06:23,567
I'M SCARED.

1433
01:06:26,167 --> 01:06:28,534
I THINK WE'RE SAFE
IN HERE WITH LIGHTNING

1434
01:06:28,567 --> 01:06:32,667
BECAUSE IT'S GOT
TIRES ON IT, RIGHT?

1435
01:06:33,601 --> 01:06:34,567
IF THIS PLANE
DIDN'T HAVE TIRES ON IT,

1436
01:06:34,601 --> 01:06:37,367
WOULD WE ALL BE FRIED?

1437
01:06:37,400 --> 01:06:40,501
I DON'T KNOW.

1438
01:06:40,868 --> 01:06:43,534
♪ WHOO HOO ♪

1439
01:06:44,367 --> 01:06:47,100
NOW, HERE ARE THE OPTIONS.
WE'RE ALL HUNGRY.

1440
01:06:47,133 --> 01:06:52,167
Woman: WE'RE PROBABLY
GOING TO BE SITTING HERE
FOR A LITTLE WHILE LONGER.

1441
01:06:52,734 --> 01:06:54,667
HELLO, TAMMY.
[SILLY VOICE]
WELL, HELLO THERE.

1442
01:06:54,701 --> 01:06:58,047
[REGULAR VOICE]
ARE YOU ANXIOUS
TO GET TO TULSA?

1443
01:06:58,067 --> 01:07:00,300
[SILLY VOICE]
SURE AS HECK AM.

1444
01:07:00,334 --> 01:07:02,868
WELL, I THINK
WE SHOULD DRIVE.

1445
01:07:02,901 --> 01:07:05,701
[REGULAR VOICE]
ME, TOO, TAM.

1446
01:07:30,567 --> 01:07:32,167
Man: SHE'S A FABULOUS SINGER.

1447
01:07:32,200 --> 01:07:34,567
UH, SHE REALLY CONNECTS
WELL WITH THE PEOPLE.

1448
01:07:34,601 --> 01:07:39,047
THIS WAS HER FIRST CONCERT
IN OVER A DECADE.

1449
01:07:39,067 --> 01:07:41,167
♪ YOU GAVE ME ♪

1450
01:07:41,200 --> 01:07:45,734
♪ THE CHANCE I NEEDED ♪

1451
01:07:45,767 --> 01:07:49,701
♪ TO START AGAIN ♪

1452
01:07:49,734 --> 01:07:50,968
Tammy: I WAS VERY,
VERY NERVOUS

1453
01:07:51,067 --> 01:07:54,100
BECAUSE I DID NOT KNOW
HOW I WOULD BE TREATED

1454
01:07:54,133 --> 01:07:55,868
AFTER SO MANY YEARS.

1455
01:07:55,901 --> 01:07:56,868
♪ AND-- ♪

1456
01:07:56,901 --> 01:07:59,701
THERE'S TOO MUCH BASS
IN THIS DOWN HERE

1457
01:07:59,734 --> 01:08:00,701
IS WHAT THE PROBLEM IS.

1458
01:08:00,734 --> 01:08:03,334
ALL I'M HEARING IS
BOOM BOOM BOOM BOOM BOOM.

1459
01:08:03,367 --> 01:08:06,200
David: THERE'S AN ELDERLY LADY
IN MY DAD'S CHURCH,

1460
01:08:06,234 --> 01:08:08,968
AND WHEN SHE FOUND OUT
THAT TAMMY FAYE

1461
01:08:09,067 --> 01:08:10,801
WAS GOING TO BE PREACHING
AT BROTHER DAVID'S CHURCH,

1462
01:08:10,834 --> 01:08:13,067
SHE SAID, "WHY IS SHE
COMING HERE?"

1463
01:08:13,100 --> 01:08:15,734
SHE JUST HAPPENED TO BE
STANDING IN THE RIGHT PLACE

1464
01:08:15,767 --> 01:08:17,567
WHILE TAMMY FAYE WAS
COMING OUT OF HER ROOM

1465
01:08:17,601 --> 01:08:20,334
GETTING READY
TO GO ON STAGE AND SING,

1466
01:08:20,367 --> 01:08:22,334
AND I DIDN'T SAY A WORD.

1467
01:08:22,367 --> 01:08:23,934
Tammy: HI,
HOW ARE YOU TODAY?

1468
01:08:23,968 --> 01:08:27,067
I'M FINE.
HOW ARE YOU, DARLIN'?

1469
01:08:27,100 --> 01:08:28,067
GOD BLESS YOU.
BLESS YOUR HEART.

1470
01:08:28,100 --> 01:08:29,300
BLESS YOUR HEART.

1471
01:08:29,334 --> 01:08:32,300
David: THE NEXT DAY
THIS LADY WAS SITTING
ON THE SECOND ROW,

1472
01:08:32,334 --> 01:08:36,047
JUST WITH THIS BIG OL'--
I THINK THEY'RE HER OWN
TEETH, BY THE WAY, TOO--

1473
01:08:36,067 --> 01:08:37,968
THIS BIG OL' SET OF TEETH
AND JUST SMILING

1474
01:08:38,067 --> 01:08:41,567
AND JUST ROOTING TAMMY ON
AND RUBBING HER ON THE BACK
AND PATTING HER.

1475
01:08:41,601 --> 01:08:42,801
SO TALKING ABOUT
RESERVATIONS,

1476
01:08:42,834 --> 01:08:44,667
WHY DO CHRISTIANS
HAVE RESERVATIONS?

1477
01:08:44,701 --> 01:08:46,334
BECAUSE THEY DON'T KNOW HER.

1478
01:08:46,367 --> 01:08:47,734
Announcer:
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN,

1479
01:08:47,767 --> 01:08:51,601
TONIGHT'S SPECIAL GUEST:
TAMMY FAYE.

1480
01:09:00,534 --> 01:09:01,501
Tammy Faye: WHEN I WALKED IN

1481
01:09:01,534 --> 01:09:04,047
AND WAS RECEIVED
WITH SO MUCH LOVE

1482
01:09:04,067 --> 01:09:06,868
AND GENUINELY, THEY SEEMED
HAPPY TO SEE ME,

1483
01:09:06,901 --> 01:09:09,601
WHICH I WAS GENUINELY
HAPPY TO BE BACK

1484
01:09:09,634 --> 01:09:11,701
WHERE I ONCE BELONGED.

1485
01:09:11,734 --> 01:09:13,200
GOSH.

1486
01:09:14,734 --> 01:09:15,834
I NEED A KLEENEX.
HA HA.

1487
01:09:15,868 --> 01:09:22,868
♪ GLORY, GLORY, HALLELUJAH ♪

1488
01:09:23,067 --> 01:09:30,067
♪ GLORY, GLORY, HALLELUJAH ♪

1489
01:09:31,601 --> 01:09:38,267
♪ GLORY, GLORY HALLELUJAH ♪

1490
01:09:38,300 --> 01:09:45,300
♪ HIS TRUTH IS MARCHING ON ♪

1491
01:09:47,167 --> 01:09:54,167
♪ HIS TRUTH IS MARCHING ON ♪

1492
01:10:01,901 --> 01:10:02,868
THANK YOU, LORD,

1493
01:10:02,901 --> 01:10:05,133
FOR THE UNITED STATES
OF AMERICA!

1494
01:10:05,167 --> 01:10:07,567
WE PRAY FOR OUR PRESIDENT,
O FATHER.

1495
01:10:07,601 --> 01:10:12,667
WE THANK YOU, LORD,
THAT WE LIVE IN THIS
WONDERFUL COUNTRY.

1496
01:10:12,701 --> 01:10:16,267
GOD BLESS AMERICA!

1497
01:10:16,300 --> 01:10:18,567
HALLELUJAH.

1498
01:10:18,601 --> 01:10:19,801
OH, YES.

1499
01:10:19,834 --> 01:10:22,234
Tammy Faye: IN
ANCIENT CIVILIZATION,

1500
01:10:22,267 --> 01:10:25,868
IF YOU MURDERED SOMEBODY,
THEY DIDN'T PUT YOU IN JAIL.

1501
01:10:25,901 --> 01:10:28,400
THEY DID SOMETHING FAR WORSE.

1502
01:10:28,434 --> 01:10:31,367
THEY TOOK THE PERSON
THAT YOU MURDERED

1503
01:10:31,400 --> 01:10:32,968
AND STUCK HIM ON YOUR BACK.

1504
01:10:33,067 --> 01:10:35,734
CAN YOU IMAGINE
WHAT THAT WOULD BE LIKE

1505
01:10:35,767 --> 01:10:39,467
TO HAVE A DEAD PERSON
STRAPPED TO YOUR BACK?

1506
01:10:39,501 --> 01:10:41,367
WELL, THE FIRST THING
THAT STARTS HAPPENING,

1507
01:10:41,400 --> 01:10:44,734
THEY START DECAYING.

1508
01:10:44,767 --> 01:10:47,434
OH, GOSH, AND THEY START
SMELLING BAD

1509
01:10:47,467 --> 01:10:49,047
AND THEN BUGS GET ON THEM.

1510
01:10:49,067 --> 01:10:51,767
YOU KNOW, WHAT DO THEY CALL
THOSE THINGS THAT EAT THEM?

1511
01:10:51,801 --> 01:10:53,701
MAGGOTS! OOH!
MAGGOTS! MAGGOTS!

1512
01:10:53,734 --> 01:10:57,667
I HAD JERRY FALWELL STRAPPED
ON MY BACK FOR A LONG TIME.

1513
01:10:57,701 --> 01:11:00,901
HE WAS ON MY BACK
STRAPPED SO TIGHTLY TO ME

1514
01:11:00,934 --> 01:11:02,767
I COULDN'T--
I COULDN'T BREATHE.

1515
01:11:02,801 --> 01:11:04,100
I COULD HARDLY EAT.

1516
01:11:04,133 --> 01:11:05,767
I HAD A HARD TIME SLEEPING.

1517
01:11:05,801 --> 01:11:09,167
I WAS MISERABLE.
HE WAS DESTROYING MY LIFE.

1518
01:11:09,200 --> 01:11:11,167
JERRY FALWELL WAS KILLING ME

1519
01:11:11,200 --> 01:11:14,300
ALL BECAUSE I WAS SO ANGRY
AT SOMEONE I COULDN'T FORGET.

1520
01:11:14,334 --> 01:11:17,567
NOW, WAS IT HURTING
JERRY FALWELL THAT
I WAS ANGRY?

1521
01:11:17,601 --> 01:11:19,200
HA HA HA HA. HE'S DEAD.

1522
01:11:19,234 --> 01:11:22,601
THE ONLY ONE IT WAS KILLING
WAS TAMMY FAYE,

1523
01:11:22,634 --> 01:11:25,400
AND ONE DAY, I GAVE
JERRY FALWELL TO THE LORD.

1524
01:11:25,434 --> 01:11:31,634
AND I SAID, "LORD, THERE'S
NOT A THING I CAN DO ABOUT
WHAT HAPPENED YESTERDAY.

1525
01:11:31,667 --> 01:11:36,567
"IT'S GONE. I CAN'T DO A THING
ABOUT WHAT JERRY FALWELL DID

1526
01:11:36,601 --> 01:11:38,434
"TO HERITAGE U.S.A. AND PTL.

1527
01:11:38,467 --> 01:11:39,734
"THAT'S ALL OVER,

1528
01:11:39,767 --> 01:11:42,267
"BUT I CAN DO SOMETHING
ABOUT MYSELF

1529
01:11:42,300 --> 01:11:44,868
AND THE WAY I FEEL."

1530
01:11:49,734 --> 01:11:51,334
RuPaul: THANKSGIVING, 1998.

1531
01:11:51,367 --> 01:11:54,367
WITH JUST A FEW MONTHS TO GO
TILL ROE'S RELEASE,

1532
01:11:54,400 --> 01:11:55,868
TAMMY RETURNS
TO HERITAGE U.S.A.

1533
01:11:55,901 --> 01:12:02,901
FOR THE FIRST TIME SINCE
SHE AND JIM LOST THEIR
PTL MINISTRY IN 1987.

1534
01:12:03,501 --> 01:12:06,667
SINCE BANKRUPTCY,
THE 2,200 ACRE COMPLEX

1535
01:12:06,701 --> 01:12:09,934
HAS LAIN EMPTY
AND ABANDONED.

1536
01:12:12,601 --> 01:12:16,400
♪ ON THE PAGES OF MY MIND ♪

1537
01:12:16,434 --> 01:12:21,067
♪ LORD, I OFTEN FIND ♪

1538
01:12:21,901 --> 01:12:24,501
♪ MEMORIES ♪

1539
01:12:26,501 --> 01:12:29,467
♪ OF THE TEARS I'VE CRIED ♪

1540
01:12:29,501 --> 01:12:32,467
♪ OF THE DAYS GONE BY ♪

1541
01:12:32,501 --> 01:12:36,801
♪ OF THE PAIN I'VE SEEN ♪

1542
01:12:39,067 --> 01:12:45,567
♪ OH, I TRIED TO UNDERSTAND
WITH A FRIEND'S HELPING HAND ♪

1543
01:12:45,601 --> 01:12:48,634
♪ IT SEEMED FUTILITY... ♪

1544
01:12:48,667 --> 01:12:53,801
Tammy Faye: JIM WOULD HAVE
NEVER ALLOWED...

1545
01:12:53,834 --> 01:12:56,467
A CHAIR LIKE THIS...

1546
01:12:56,868 --> 01:12:57,834
TO SIT.

1547
01:12:57,868 --> 01:13:02,133
AT HERITAGE U.S.A.
IT WOULD HAVE BEEN PAINTED.

1548
01:13:02,167 --> 01:13:04,367
HE NEVER ALLOWED
A LIGHT BULB TO BE OUT,

1549
01:13:04,400 --> 01:13:06,901
HE NEVER ALLOWED
A DIRTY REST ROOM,

1550
01:13:06,934 --> 01:13:10,133
HE NEVER ALLOWED
GRASS TO GROW UNCUT,

1551
01:13:10,167 --> 01:13:12,734
AND HE WOULD HAVE NEVER
ALLOWED THIS.

1552
01:13:12,767 --> 01:13:17,200
WHEN I LOOK AT THIS CHAIR
RUSTED AWAY,

1553
01:13:17,234 --> 01:13:20,501
THAT'S SORT OF WHAT'S
HAPPENED TO HERITAGE U.S.A.,

1554
01:13:20,534 --> 01:13:25,634
AND HOW I WOULD LOVE
TO PUT A FRESH COAT
OF PAINT ON IT...

1555
01:13:25,667 --> 01:13:27,434
AND MAKE IT LIVE AGAIN...

1556
01:13:27,467 --> 01:13:29,133
[SOBS]

1557
01:13:29,167 --> 01:13:35,133
BUT UNFORTUNATELY,
I CAN'T DO THAT.

1558
01:13:36,434 --> 01:13:40,267
THIS MORNING, WHEN I
WAS NEEDING SOME COMFORT,

1559
01:13:40,300 --> 01:13:43,601
I TURNED TO MY FAVORITE
SCRIPTURE, PSALMS 91.

1560
01:13:43,634 --> 01:13:47,467
"HE THAT DWELLETH IN THE
SECRET PLACE OF THE MOST HIGH

1561
01:13:47,501 --> 01:13:50,701
SHALL ABIDE UNDER THE SHADOW
OF THE ALMIGHTY."

1562
01:13:50,734 --> 01:13:53,067
THIS IS THE PART I LIKE.

1563
01:13:59,067 --> 01:13:59,968
[REPRESSING TEARS]

1564
01:14:00,067 --> 01:14:03,167
"HE SHALL COVER THEE
WITH HIS FEATHERS

1565
01:14:03,200 --> 01:14:08,567
AND UNDER HIS WINGS
SHALT THOU TRUST."

1566
01:14:09,901 --> 01:14:12,534
"BECAUSE HE HAS SET
HIS LOVE UPON ME,

1567
01:14:12,567 --> 01:14:14,567
"THEREFORE
WILL I DELIVER HIM.

1568
01:14:14,601 --> 01:14:18,801
"I WILL SET HIM ON HIGH
BECAUSE HE HATH KNOWN MY NAME.

1569
01:14:18,834 --> 01:14:22,801
"HE SHALL CALL UPON ME
AND I WILL ANSWER HIM.

1570
01:14:22,834 --> 01:14:24,767
"I WILL
BE WITH HIM IN TROUBLE.

1571
01:14:24,801 --> 01:14:27,067
"I WILL DELIVER HIM
AND HONOR HIM,

1572
01:14:27,100 --> 01:14:30,434
"AND WITH LONG LIFE,
I WILL SATISFY HIM

1573
01:14:30,467 --> 01:14:33,767
AND SHOW HIM MY SALVATION."

1574
01:14:38,067 --> 01:14:43,901
I WILL HUG ROE TODAY
FOR THE FIRST TIME IN 2 YEARS

1575
01:14:43,934 --> 01:14:48,300
WITHOUT HAVING PEOPLE
STANDING THERE WATCHING ME.

1576
01:15:06,834 --> 01:15:08,801
Roe: I'M STILL NUMB,
REALLY.

1577
01:15:08,834 --> 01:15:12,267
YOU KNOW, BEING AWAY
FROM YOUR WIFE
AND FAMILY

1578
01:15:12,300 --> 01:15:14,334
IS REALLY HARD.

1579
01:15:14,367 --> 01:15:18,334
IT'S JUST...YOU KNOW,
I JUST DON'T KNOW
HOW TO SAY IT

1580
01:15:18,367 --> 01:15:20,767
OTHER THAN THAT.

1581
01:15:22,767 --> 01:15:26,634
WELL, WE GOTTA GO
GET TO KNOW EACH OTHER AGAIN.

1582
01:15:26,667 --> 01:15:28,367
GOOD-BYE.

1583
01:15:28,767 --> 01:15:32,634
Tammy Faye: I'M JUST
A SMALL TOWN GIRL AT HEART

1584
01:15:32,667 --> 01:15:36,667
AND I WANT TO GO BACK
TO THE TREES AND THE GRASS

1585
01:15:36,701 --> 01:15:43,167
AND THE FLOWERS AND MY KIDS
AND MY GRANDKIDS.

1586
01:15:43,200 --> 01:15:46,934
BECAUSE WHEN YOU GET DOWN TO IT,
THAT'S REALLY ALL THERE IS.

1587
01:15:46,968 --> 01:15:51,133
THAT'S WHAT COUNTS IN LIFE,
AND I'VE LEARNED THAT.

1588
01:15:51,167 --> 01:15:53,334
IT'S NOT WHAT YOU HAVE

1589
01:15:53,367 --> 01:15:55,634
AND--AND--AND STUFF.

1590
01:15:55,667 --> 01:15:58,167
IT'S PEOPLE THAT COUNT.

1591
01:16:06,634 --> 01:16:13,634
♪ DON'T GIVE UP
ON THE BRINK OF A MIRACLE ♪

1592
01:16:14,767 --> 01:16:21,767
♪ DON'T GIVE IN WHILE
HE'S STILL ON THE THRONE ♪

1593
01:16:23,067 --> 01:16:30,067
♪ DON'T GIVE UP
ON THE BRINK OF A MIRACLE ♪

1594
01:16:31,067 --> 01:16:33,200
♪ DON'T GIVE UP ♪

1595
01:16:33,234 --> 01:16:40,047
♪ REMEMBER YOU'RE NOT ALONE ♪

1596
01:16:40,067 --> 01:16:41,434
♪ WELL, THE DEVIL IS A THIEF ♪

1597
01:16:41,467 --> 01:16:47,834
♪ AND HE SENDS ALL THOSE
TROUBLES TO CONFOUND YOU ♪

1598
01:16:47,868 --> 01:16:49,801
♪ AND HE LIES AND SAYS
THIS TIME ♪

1599
01:16:49,834 --> 01:16:56,701
♪ THERE'S NO WAY YOU
CAN FIND TO MAKE IT THROUGH ♪

1600
01:16:56,734 --> 01:16:58,534
♪ GOD'S WORD IS TRUE ♪

1601
01:16:58,567 --> 01:17:00,934
♪ THE DEVIL IS THE LORD'S ♪

1602
01:17:00,968 --> 01:17:02,434
♪ DON'T GIVE IN TO FEAR ♪

1603
01:17:02,467 --> 01:17:05,047
♪ THINK ON THINGS
THAT ARE PURE ♪

1604
01:17:05,067 --> 01:17:06,534
♪ AND PRAISE THE LORD ♪

1605
01:17:06,567 --> 01:17:11,567
♪ YOUR MIRACLE IS HERE ♪

1606
01:17:11,601 --> 01:17:18,601
♪ DON'T GIVE UP
ON THE BRINK OF A MIRACLE ♪

1607
01:17:20,434 --> 01:17:21,834
♪ DON'T YOU GIVE IN ♪

1608
01:17:21,868 --> 01:17:28,367
♪ GOD IS STILL ON HIS THRONE ♪

1609
01:17:28,400 --> 01:17:29,567
♪ DON'T GIVE UP ♪

1610
01:17:29,601 --> 01:17:36,467
♪ YOU'RE ON THE BRINK
OF YOUR MIRACLE ♪

1611
01:17:36,501 --> 01:17:37,834
♪ DON'T GIVE UP ♪

1612
01:17:37,868 --> 01:17:44,200
♪ REMEMBER YOU'RE NOT ALONE ♪

1613
01:17:44,234 --> 01:17:45,701
♪ NOW, DON'T GIVE UP ♪

1614
01:17:45,734 --> 01:17:52,501
♪ ON THE BRINK
OF A MIRACLE ♪

1615
01:17:52,534 --> 01:17:53,767
♪ DON'T GIVE IN ♪

1616
01:17:53,801 --> 01:18:00,167
♪ REMEMBER YOU'RE NOT ALONE ♪

1617
01:18:00,200 --> 01:18:02,200
♪ OH, DON'T GIVE IN ♪

1618
01:18:02,234 --> 01:18:09,234
♪ REMEMBER YOU'RE NOT ALONE ♪

1619
01:18:10,067 --> 01:18:12,467
♪ YOU'RE NOT ALONE! ♪

1620
01:18:12,501 --> 01:18:14,501
COME ON, PEOPLE,
DON'T YOU DARE GIVE UP!
